---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import CaseIntro from '../../components/CaseIntro.astro';
import { url } from '../../lib/url.js';

// TODO(Francesca): Sky timeline and team; replace the .visual-slot with a before/after visual.
const steps = [
  { n: '01', title: 'Audit', text: 'Every touchpoint checked against UNI EN 301 549, criterion by criterion.' },
  { n: '02', title: 'Design fixes', text: 'Contrast, focus states, labels, reading order, touch targets. Fixed in the design first, with annotations for the developers.' },
  { n: '03', title: 'Review', text: 'Design and development reviewed against the criteria, so the fixes actually made it to production.' },
  { n: '04', title: 'Training', text: 'Sessions with the developers on the why, not only the how. Bugs stop coming back when the people writing the code know the reason.' },
];
---
<Base title="Accessibility that sticks · Francesca Folkmer"
  description="Two accessibility projects, two approaches: at Sky, a measured jump from 50% to 85% compliance; at Crédit Agricole, accessibility moved into the design, before the code.">
  <article class="container case">
    <CaseIntro
      tags={['Accessibility', 'Media', 'Banking', 'Developer training']}
      title="Accessibility that sticks"
      facts={[['Projects', 'Sky (Sep 2025 - Oct 2026), Crédit Agricole (2025 - Now)'], ['Role', 'Accessibility lead & UX/UI Designer'], ['Standards', 'WCAG 2.2, UNI EN 301 549']]}
    >
      <Fragment slot="media"><img src={url('/img/a11y-cover.svg')} alt="An illustration of accessibility in Sky colours: a Tab key, braille dots, a crossed-out eye, an ear, a screen reader, a microphone, text sizes and a cursor clicking HERE." width="1328" height="520" /></Fragment>
      <p>Two projects, two approaches. At Sky I audited and fixed seven live touchpoints, and we measured it: compliance went from <b>50% to 85%</b>, with <b>two touchpoints at 100%</b>. At Crédit Agricole, 300+ defects kept coming back, so the approach changed: accessibility now goes <b>into the design</b>, before a line of code.</p>
    </CaseIntro>

    <header class="chapter reveal" aria-labelledby="ch-sky">
      <h2 id="ch-sky" class="h2 chapter__title">Sky</h2>
      <p class="chapter__lead">Seven touchpoints already live: audit, fix, review, teach, and measure everything. September 2025 to October 2026.</p>
    </header>

    <section class="measure reveal" aria-labelledby="measure">
      <div class="measure__text">
        <p class="eyebrow">The starting point</p>
        <h3 id="measure" class="h2">Half accessible isn't accessible</h3>
        <p>Seven Sky touchpoints met about half of the applicable criteria of UNI EN 301 549, the European standard that includes WCAG. We measured one simple thing: criteria passed ÷ applicable criteria. Easy to repeat, easy to explain to people who have never heard of WCAG.</p>
      </div>
      <img class="measure__img" src={url('/img/sky-code.webp')} width="1273" height="607" loading="lazy"
        alt="A Sky checkout page next to the browser developer tools, open on its HTML: where each criterion gets checked." />
    </section>

    <section class="steps" aria-labelledby="how">
      <div class="results__intro reveal">
        <p class="eyebrow">What I did</p>
        <h3 id="how" class="h2">Audit, fix, review, teach</h3>
      </div>
      <ol class="steps__list">
        {steps.map((s) => (
          <li class="step reveal">
            <span class="step__n" aria-hidden="true">{s.n}</span>
            <h3>{s.title}</h3>
            <p>{s.text}</p>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="results" aria-labelledby="results">
      <div class="results__intro reveal">
        <p class="eyebrow">What changed</p>
        <h3 id="results" class="h2">Seven touchpoints later</h3>
      </div>
      <div class="results__grid">
        <div class="result result--stat reveal">
          <p class="result__num">85%</p>
          <p><span class="result__label">Measured</span>UNI EN 301 549 compliance across the seven touchpoints.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="result result--stat reveal">
          <p class="result__num">2</p>
          <p><span class="result__label">Touchpoints</span>pass every applicable criterion.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="result reveal">
          <b>A team that knows why</b>
          <p>Developers trained on accessibility, so new features start from a better place.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <header class="chapter reveal" aria-labelledby="ch-ca">
      <h2 id="ch-ca" class="h2 chapter__title">Crédit Agricole</h2>
      <p class="chapter__lead">A banking app with 300+ accessibility defects. Fixing them at the end stopped working, so the approach changed: we step in directly in the design.</p>
    </header>

    <section class="split" aria-labelledby="ca-problem">
      <div class="split__text reveal">
        <div class="split__title">
          <p class="eyebrow">The problem</p>
          <h3 id="ca-problem" class="h2">We didn't have a bug problem. We had a process problem.</h3>
        </div>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>The audit of the app's core templates found <b>over 300 accessibility defects</b>. The workflow was <b>"fix it at the end"</b>: design, develop, test, and only then discover what doesn't work. Which meant:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><b>Costly revisions:</b> endless back and forth between designers and developers.</li>
            <li><b>Delayed releases:</b> UAT kept getting blocked by critical accessibility issues.</li>
            <li><b>Compliance risk:</b> no way to guarantee an inclusive experience for everyone.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="split__media defects reveal" aria-hidden="true">
        <img class="defects__num" src={url('/img/ca-300.svg')} alt="" />
        <p class="defects__word">defect</p>
        <div class="defects__notes">
          {[0, 1, 2, 3].map((i) => (
            <div class={`note note--${i}`}>
              <span class="note__tag">WCAG 1.4.3</span>
              <span class="note__text">The contrast between the label and the background is not sufficient. It has to be at least 4.5:1.</span>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="split split--media-first" aria-labelledby="strategy">
      <div class="split__media reveal">
        <img class="draw-in" src={url("/img/ca-strategy.webp")} alt="A monthly spending card before and after: the accessible version has clearer labels, contrast and states. Label: make every component accessible." width="629" height="480" />
      </div>
      <div class="split__text reveal">
        <div class="split__title">
          <p class="eyebrow">The idea</p>
          <h3 id="strategy" class="h2">From patching to prevention</h3>
        </div>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>The issues kept coming back because they were born in the <b>UI kit itself</b>.</p>
          <p>So I proposed a shift: from a standard UI kit to an <b>accessibility-first design system</b>. Developers receive components that are already compliant, and the room for error gets a lot smaller. In other words: shift left.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="split" aria-labelledby="solution">
      <div class="split__text reveal">
        <div class="split__title">
          <p class="eyebrow">What we built</p>
          <h3 id="solution" class="h2">The Accessibility Kit</h3>
        </div>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>A handoff framework that tells developers exactly how each component has to behave:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><b>Semantic annotations:</b> screen reader labels, roles and traits for every element.</li>
            <li><b>Focus order:</b> the logical path for keyboard and assistive technology users.</li>
            <li><b>Redlines and touch targets:</b> minimum hit areas and contrast ratios.</li>
            <li><b>States:</b> hover, focus, active, disabled. Every state defined, no guessing.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>The kit is being rolled out screen by screen. The <b>target</b>: about 80% fewer accessibility bugs in UAT.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="split__media reveal">
        <img src={url("/img/ca-solution.webp")} alt="A mortgage screen annotated with accessibility labels: A1 alternative text on the image, #1 back button with its aria-label." width="542" height="483" />
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="retro reveal" aria-labelledby="retro">
      <h2 id="retro" class="h2">What I learned</h2>
      <p>Fixing is the easy part. What makes accessibility stick is moving it earlier, into the components, and explaining the why to the people who write the code. And talking about it in the language of the business: fewer blocked releases, less rework, lower risk.</p>
    </section>

  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .chapter { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px; padding-top: clamp(32px, 4vw, 56px); border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .chapter__lead { font-size: var(--fs-lead); color: var(--ink-2); max-width: 52ch; }

  .visual-slot {
    aspect-ratio: 540 / 400; border-radius: var(--radius-l);
    border: 2px dashed var(--line); background: var(--surface);
    display: grid; place-items: center; color: var(--ink-2); font-size: var(--fs-small); text-align: center; padding: 16px;
  }
  .visual-slot--wide { aspect-ratio: 1328 / 520; margin-top: 32px; }

  .measure { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 654fr) minmax(0, 540fr); gap: clamp(32px, 7vw, 134px); align-items: center; }
  .measure__img { width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; filter: drop-shadow(0 12px 32px rgba(0,0,0,.12)); }
  .measure__text { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px; }

  .steps { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 32px; }
  .steps__list { list-style: none; padding: 0; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 24px; }
  .step { background: var(--surface); border-radius: var(--radius-l); padding: 24px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px; }
  .step h3 { font-size: var(--fs-lead); font-weight: 600; }
  .step__n { font-size: var(--fs-caption); font-weight: 600; color: var(--sage-text); letter-spacing: .06em; }
  .steps__list .step:nth-child(2) { transition-delay: .1s; }
  .steps__list .step:nth-child(3) { transition-delay: .2s; }
  .steps__list .step:nth-child(4) { transition-delay: .3s; }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .measure { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .steps__list { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .visual-slot--wide { aspect-ratio: 4 / 3; }
  }
</style>

<style>
  .ca-hero__phones { position: absolute; top: 4.6%; left: 50%; height: 91%; width: auto !important; object-fit: contain !important; transform: translateX(-2%); }
  .ca-hero__title {
    position: absolute; left: 3%; top: 33%; width: 42%;
    color: var(--white); font-weight: 600; font-size: clamp(24px, 4.7vw, 62px); line-height: 1.2; text-align: center;
  }

  /* 300+ defects: notes fan out when the section enters */
  .defects { aspect-ratio: 540 / 480; }
  .defects__num { position: absolute; left: 9.5%; top: 28.5%; width: 71.6%; }
  .defects__word { position: absolute; left: 9.3%; top: 52%; font-size: clamp(36px, 4.8vw, 64px); font-weight: 500; color: #037787; }
  .defects__notes { position: absolute; left: 50%; top: 47%; width: 34.2%; }
  .note {
    position: absolute; inset: 0 auto auto 0; width: 100%;
    background: var(--white); border-radius: var(--radius-m); padding: 8px;
    box-shadow: 0 1px 1px rgba(0,0,0,.3), 0 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.15);
    display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px;
    font-family: Inter, system-ui, sans-serif; font-size: var(--fs-meta); line-height: 1.5; color: #2c2c2c;
    transition: transform var(--dur-story) var(--ease-spring);
  }
  .note__tag { background: #037787; color: var(--white); border-radius: 4px; padding: 0 7px; font-weight: 500; font-size: var(--fs-meta); }
  .reveal.is-in .note--0 { transform: rotate(12.85deg) translate(-4%, 8%); transition-delay: .15s; }
  .reveal.is-in .note--1 { transform: rotate(-9deg); transition-delay: .25s; }
  .reveal.is-in .note--2 { transform: rotate(6.87deg) translate(2%, 2%); transition-delay: .35s; }
  .note--3 { z-index: 1; }

  .draw-in { clip-path: inset(0 100% 0 0); transition: clip-path var(--dur-story) var(--ease-out) .2s; }
  .reveal.is-in .draw-in { clip-path: inset(0 0 0 0); }
  :global(.no-js) .draw-in { clip-path: none; }
</style>
